---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import catalog from '../data/webhook-catalog.json';
const title = 'A small signal, a useful action';
const description = 'A friendly field guide to webhooks, with an offline example and 100 proposed event contracts for the PointCast ecosystem.';
const categories = [...new Set(catalog.contracts.map(c => c.category))];
const jsonLd = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'TechArticle',headline:title,description,url:'https://pointcast.xyz/webhooks/',datePublished:'2026-10-27',author:{'@type':'Organization',name:'PointCast'},publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'PointCast'},image:'https://pointcast.xyz/webhook-field-guide/signal.svg'};
---
<BlockLayout title={title} description={description} image="/webhook-field-guide/signal.svg" imageWidth={1200} imageHeight={760} imageAlt="An illustrated signal connecting two buildings" jsonLd={jsonLd} isolated includeManifest={false}>
  <div class="guide">
    <nav class="top" aria-label="Field guide navigation"><a href="/">← POINTCAST</a><span>FIELD GUIDE / OCTOBER 2026</span><a href="#catalog">THE 100 ↓</a></nav>
    <header class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">POINTCAST FIELD NOTES / 01</p><h1>A small signal,<br/><em>a useful action.</em></h1><p class="dek">What if the things we make could tell each other when something changes?</p><p class="byline">A FRIENDLY GUIDE TO WEBHOOKS &nbsp; / &nbsp; 8 MIN READ</p><a class="button" href="#start">Start with the idea <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div><figure><img src="/webhook-field-guide/signal.svg" alt="An illustrated message traveling between two buildings" width="1200" height="760"/><figcaption>ILLUSTRATION 01 / THE SIGNAL & THE NEIGHBOR</figcaption></figure></header>
    <section class="intro" id="start"><p class="lead">A webhook is a little note that says: <em>“Something happened.”</em></p><div><p>Imagine a story is published. Instead of another site checking every minute for news, the publisher can send a message when the story is ready. A receiver checks the message and decides what to do next.</p><p>That note is a webhook: an HTTP message sent by one system to another when an event occurs. The message is useful because the two sides agree in advance on its shape, its sender, and what it means.</p><p>Not every signal is a webhook. An <strong>internal event</strong> stays inside a system; <strong>scheduled polling</strong> asks for changes on a timer. A <strong>demo</strong> shows an idea without a connection. An <strong>implemented adapter</strong> is code for a particular integration; a <strong>live connection</strong> is actually configured and operating. These are different stages.</p></div></section>
    <section class="route"><p class="eyebrow">THE JOURNEY / THREE PARTS</p><h2>From here to there.</h2><p>A sender notices a change. A small envelope describes it. A receiver verifies it before deciding whether to act.</p><img src="/webhook-field-guide/route.svg" alt="Sender: something happens. Message: a small envelope. Receiver: verify, then act." width="1200" height="300"/><p class="fine">Delivery can happen more than once. The receiver needs a durable way to recognize an event it has already handled.</p></section>
    <section class="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">TRY IT / NOTHING IS SENT</p><h2 id="demo-title">Open the envelope.</h2><p>Choose any proposed contract, edit its fictional example, and check its shape in your browser. It does not publish a story, contact a server, or store your input.</p><p class="fine">The check is educational; a real receiver also needs authentication, freshness checks, durable deduplication and authorization.</p></div><div class="terminal"><label for="demo-contract">PROPOSED CONTRACT</label><select id="demo-contract">{catalog.contracts.map(c => <option value={c.id}>{c.id}</option>)}</select><label for="envelope">EXAMPLE ENVELOPE / JSON</label><textarea id="envelope" rows="10" spellcheck="false">{JSON.stringify(catalog.contracts[0].example, null, 2)}</textarea><button id="check" type="button">Check example ↗</button><p id="check-result" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to check locally.</p></div></section>
    <section class="reality"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE HONEST STATUS</p><h2>100 ideas.<br/><em>Zero live connections.</em></h2></div><div><p>Below is a map of proposed internal events across ten parts of the ecosystem. These are contracts to design and review—not a claim that the sites already emit them or that a webhook connection is active.</p><p>Each entry names a possible source, destination and action. No connector has credentials, a schedule, or a public relay here. Public changes require human review. External services that need new access remain blocked.</p><p>Our neutral versioned envelope could later refer to a receipt after separate review. A message or receipt alone does not establish blockchain finality.</p><a href="/webhooks.json">Read the machine-readable catalog ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="catalog" id="catalog"><div class="catalog-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A CATALOG FOR A CONNECTED TOWN</p><h2>One hundred<br/>possible signals.</h2></div><p>Search by name, action, or place. Open a row to see the proposal. All are <strong>planned and disabled</strong>.</p></div><div class="filters"><label for="search">SEARCH THE CATALOG<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Try “lesson” or “coffee”" autocomplete="off"/></label><label for="category">PLACE<select id="category"><option value="">All places</option>{categories.map(c => <option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></label><p id="count" role="status" aria-live="polite">100 proposed contracts</p></div><div class="rows" id="rows">{catalog.contracts.map((c,i) => <details data-row data-category={c.category} data-search={`${c.id} ${c.category} ${c.event} ${c.action} ${c.source} ${c.destination}`.toLowerCase()}><summary><span class="row-number">{String(i+1).padStart(3,'0')}</span><span><span class="row-category">{c.category}</span><strong>{c.action}</strong><code>{c.id}</code></span><span class="row-status">PLANNED <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></span></summary><div class="row-body"><p><b>When:</b> {c.event.replaceAll('.', ' ')} <br/><b>From:</b> {c.source} → <b>To:</b> {c.destination}</p><p><b>Trigger:</b> proposed internal event · <b>Connection:</b> disabled · <b>Privacy:</b> public metadata only</p><p><b>Approval:</b> {c.approval}. <b>Dependencies:</b> {c.dependencies.join(', ')}.</p><p><b>Deduplication:</b> {c.deduplication}. <b>Cost:</b> {c.cost}.</p><p><a href="/webhooks.json">Schema and example in JSON ↗</a></p></div></details>)}</div><p id="empty" hidden>No proposals match that search. Try a different word or place.</p><noscript><p>All 100 entries are available above. Search and filtering require JavaScript.</p></noscript></section>
    <section class="closing"><p class="eyebrow">A GOOD SIGNAL KNOWS ITS LIMITS</p><h2>Small messages.<br/><em>Thoughtful connections.</em></h2><p>A useful integration is specific about what happened, careful with what it shares, and clear about who gets to decide what happens next.</p><div><a href="/webhooks.json">JSON catalog ↗</a><a href="/agent-native-publishing/">Agent-native publishing ↗</a><a href="/">Back to PointCast ↗</a></div></section>
  </div>
</BlockLayout>
<script>
  import catalog from '../data/webhook-catalog.json';
  import { previewEnvelope } from '../lib/webhook-envelope.mjs';
  const search = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#search');
  const category = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#category');
  const count = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#count');
  const empty = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#empty');
  const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-row]')];
  function filter() {
    const term = (search?.value ?? '').trim().toLowerCase(); const place = category?.value ?? ''; let n = 0;
    rows.forEach(row => { const show = (row.dataset.search ?? '').includes(term) && (!place || row.dataset.category === place); row.hidden = !show; if(show) n++; });
    if(count) count.textContent = `${n} proposed contract${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`; if(empty) empty.hidden = n !== 0;
  }
  search?.addEventListener('input', filter); category?.addEventListener('change', filter);
  const demoContract = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#demo-contract');
  demoContract?.addEventListener('change', () => {
    const selected = catalog.contracts.find(c => c.id === demoContract.value);
    const editor = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#envelope');
    if (selected && editor) editor.value = JSON.stringify(selected.example, null, 2);
    const out = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#check-result'); if (out) out.textContent = 'Ready to check locally.';
  });
  document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#check')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const selected = catalog.contracts.find(c => c.id === demoContract?.value);
    const result = previewEnvelope(document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#envelope')?.value ?? '', selected);
    const out = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#check-result'); if(out) out.textContent = result.ok ? `${result.message}\n${JSON.stringify(result.receipt, null, 2)}` : result.error;
  });
</script>
<style>
.guide{--ink:#172c25;background:#faf7eb;color:var(--ink);font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;overflow:hidden}.guide *{box-sizing:border-box}.guide a{color:inherit}.top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid;padding:20px clamp(20px,5vw,72px);font:700 10px/1.4 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.08em}.top a{text-decoration:none}.eyebrow,.byline,figcaption,.fine,.row-category,.row-status,.row-number,.filters label,.terminal label{font:700 10px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.08em}.eyebrow{color:#9b472e}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:5vw;align-items:center;padding:90px clamp(20px,5vw,72px)}h1,h2{letter-spacing:-.055em;line-height:.98;margin:0;font-weight:750}h1{font-size:clamp(52px,6.5vw,98px)}h2{font-size:clamp(40px,5vw,72px)}em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}.dek{font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,27px);line-height:1.4;max-width:27ch}.byline{margin:30px 0}.button,.terminal button{display:inline-block;background:var(--ink);color:#fff9e9!important;padding:16px 20px;text-decoration:none;border:0;font:700 12px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;cursor:pointer}.hero figure{margin:0}.hero img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid}.hero figcaption{padding-top:10px}.intro{border-top:1px solid;border-bottom:1px solid;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8vw;padding:75px clamp(20px,5vw,72px);font-size:17px;line-height:1.7}.intro p:first-child{margin-top:0}.intro .lead{font-size:clamp(30px,3.5vw,50px);line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.04em}.route{padding:85px clamp(20px,5vw,72px)}.route>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:65ch;line-height:1.6}.route img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin-top:40px;border:1px solid}.fine{letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.6;font-size:11px}.demo,.reality{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8vw;padding:80px clamp(20px,5vw,72px);line-height:1.6}.demo{background:#dbe8d2}.terminal{background:#fffaf0;border:1px solid;padding:24px;box-shadow:8px 8px 0 #172c25}.terminal label{display:block;margin-bottom:12px}.terminal select{width:100%;padding:12px;margin-bottom:20px;background:#fffaf0;color:#172c25;border:1px solid;font:13px monospace}.terminal textarea{width:100%;resize:vertical;background:#f3f0e4;color:#172c25;border:1px solid;padding:14px;font:13px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}.terminal button{margin-top:12px}.terminal p{font-size:13px;min-height:2em;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.reality{background:#172c25;color:#f7f4e8}.reality .eyebrow{color:#f3bd74}.reality a{color:#d2edbb}.catalog{padding:90px clamp(20px,5vw,72px)}.catalog-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8vw;align-items:end}.catalog-head>p{max-width:45ch;line-height:1.6}.filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;align-items:end;margin:42px 0 20px}.filters label{display:grid;gap:7px;flex:1;min-width:200px}.filters input,.filters select{width:100%;border:1px solid;background:white;color:#172c25;padding:13px;font:16px system-ui}.filters p{font:12px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}.rows{border-top:1px solid}.rows details{border-bottom:1px solid}.rows details[hidden]{display:none}.rows summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:55px 1fr auto;gap:15px;align-items:center;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;padding:20px 0}.rows summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.rows strong,.rows code,.row-category{display:block}.rows strong{font-size:20px;margin:5px 0}.rows code{font-size:11px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.row-status{white-space:nowrap}.row-status span{font-size:20px;margin-left:14px}.row-body{padding:0 0 24px 70px;max-width:85ch;line-height:1.6;font-size:14px}.closing{background:#f2c575;padding:85px clamp(20px,5vw,72px)}.closing>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:55ch;line-height:1.6}.closing div{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;margin-top:35px;font:700 12px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}.guide :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #d45b36;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.top span{display:none}.hero,.intro,.demo,.reality,.catalog-head{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:35px}.hero{padding-top:55px}.intro,.demo,.reality{padding-top:60px;padding-bottom:60px}.row-number{display:none}.rows summary{grid-template-columns:1fr auto}.row-body{padding-left:0}.row-status{font-size:9px}.row-status span{margin-left:4px}.route img{min-height:125px;object-fit:contain}.closing{padding-top:60px}}
</style>
